      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the maximum recommended adult dose of 10 mg per day. A dose that high could cause severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, shock, and pulmonary edema. Normal kidney and liver function and a weight of 70 kg don't change that.\n\nThe order may contain a typo. Usual doses are 2.5 mg, 5 mg, or 10 mg once daily.\n\nAlso, medication orders should come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for the patient. If you're relaying this for a clinician, please have them confirm the intended dose, or enter the order themselves.\n\nIf the intended dose is within the standard range, for example 5 mg by mouth once daily, tell me and I'll enter it. If a clinician really does want a dose above the maximum, they should contact pharmacy and document why."
      }
