     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order, even with your confirmation. Amlodipine 50 mg is five times the maximum daily dose, and it could seriously harm the patient. Your confirmation doesn't change that, because you aren't the prescriber of record. A licensed prescriber needs to take responsibility for an order like this.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter a standard dose.** I can enter 5 mg or 10 mg by mouth once daily as soon as you or the prescriber tell me which one.\n- **Have the treating clinician place the order.** If they think a dose above the maximum is justified, they should talk to pharmacy first and document their reasoning.\n- **Check for a transcription error.** The 50 mg may have been meant as 5 mg.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
